## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: routing binding reports can clear terminal output or insert extra report lines when configured match fields contain control characters.

## User Impact

User impact: operators can read routing reports safely without changing routing keys, stored configuration, JSON output, or ordinary Unicode text.

## Why This Change Was Made

Apply the existing terminal sanitizer at the binding command's human-readable output boundaries, including mutation summaries and conflicts. Keep the shared binding description formatter raw for JSON consumers. No config/default, protocol/schema, permission/security-policy, dependency, compatibility, or migration changes.

## Evidence

